            "created_at": "2025-09-03T20:04:18.894073+00:00",
            "notes": "Round 3 is the pivot point towards the build, you may choose to continue investing purely in [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) if you are unable to afford the important items this round, but make sure you take everything here as they are core to the build.\n\nOur power of choice is [Optimizer](item_13d41c37-8f79-4435-9d81-c9599955f6a8), this is the lifeblood of our ability to self-sustain.\n\nNext we take [Gloomgauntlet](item_76cb8fe3-3c1f-4769-a1ec-a9c2dc510ba7) and [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8). \n\nAny spare money should be spent on [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) to squeeze more value out of [Gloomgauntlet](item_76cb8fe3-3c1f-4769-a1ec-a9c2dc510ba7).\n\nYou should try to engage with at least two repair packs active at any one time, make sure you spam your abilities as much as possible whilst you are in the fight, when you land a shield bash or whip shot you extends [Packstacker](item_87b99cde-3089-42fd-86bc-6e1ebf3fe422), which extends the self heal provided by [Optimizer](item_13d41c37-8f79-4435-9d81-c9599955f6a8). And for every ability used you regenerate armor from [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8). This synergy in itself will help you outlast most tanks in the game.\n\nIf you are struggling to live you are most likely jumping in 1v100 expecting to live forever. You do not have the HP to sit in front of your entire team and absorb all the damage sent. You should try to play as if you are playing [Reinhardt](hero_a3b6ca2c-6cbd-43dc-bb78-a728e42fba49), play around corners minimize the line of sight from long range poke characters and push in when the advantage is clear.",
